      "title": "Three labels can describe one insurer",
      "narration": "Elena reviews a life insurer formed in Pennsylvania and authorized to operate in Maryland. Its shareholders own the company. Is it stock, foreign, or admitted? It can be all three. Stock describes ownership. Foreign describes where the company was formed relative to Maryland. Admitted describes authorization in Maryland. Exam questions often put these separate dimensions together. Begin by asking which dimension the question actually tests. A company's location, ownership and permission to transact business are not interchangeable labels.",
