      "title": "Where was it formed?",
      "narration": "Domicile refers to the jurisdiction of formation. For a Maryland question, an insurer formed in Maryland is domestic. One formed in another U.S. state is foreign. One formed outside the United States is alien. These terms say nothing by themselves about whether the company is licensed in Maryland. A foreign or alien insurer can be admitted. An office in Baltimore does not turn a Pennsylvania corporation into a Maryland domestic insurer. The formation jurisdiction, rather than the producer's office, controls this classification.",
